      "writtenOn": "2024-12-02T18:51:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AdminMaxTimeout is a Long, so that could be a number the converts to \u003e25 days. ConfigMaxTimeout is an Int casted to a Long, so the largest number it could represent is 25 days. If we wanted, by config, to support more than 25 days as a timeout, it would need to be stored as a Long instead of an Int. To achieve this, it would have to be stored in XML as a String, that in this java code would need to be parsed as a Long (`Long.parseLong`). I can\u0027t say whether we _need_ to support a longer max timeout, but calling out that this is a limitation imposed currently by using an Integer",
      "parentUuid": "6d9328b3_274c4e90",
      "revId": "5c547c801636b8101194f257c4c86e76d0bd1554",
